{
  "_id": "21128c087658aa2a",
  "name": "The Motor City Sentinel",
  "type": "character",
  "img": "systems/heroic5e/assets/characters/motor-city-sentinel/portrait.png",
  "system": {
    "biography": "<h2>Jake Fulton</h2><p>A Detroit mechanic and body-shop owner transformed by the Pulse into a powered-suit hero, using armor, gadgets, and machine interface abilities to protect the city.</p><h3>Backstory</h3><p>Jake Fulton is a Detroit native and lifelong Pistons, Tigers, Red Wings, and Lions fan. He learned shop work in high school, fixed cars and small engines around the neighborhood, and grew that skill into a solid repair business. He and his close high-school friends were ice fishing when the Pulse happened. He now balances hero work with caring for his nephew Colton after Chloe and Kyle died in a car wreck.</p><h3>Costume</h3><p>A Detroit-inspired powered armor suit built from automotive and machine-shop parts.</p>",
    "notes": "<p>Technology and machine systems<br>Science and mechanical problem-solving<br>Vehicles and high-speed handling<br>Acrobatics and armored mobility<br>Insight and tactical reads<br>Pattern recognition</p><p>Mechanic/body shop work; cars and small engine equipment; powered armor fabrication and repair.</p><p>Level 1: Precision Strike<br>Level 1: Exploit the Opening</p><p>Armor grants +2 to all Active Defense rolls while armored.<br>Armor grants Resistance: Bludgeoning.<br>Machine Interface grants Advantage on Technology checks.<br>Enhanced Recovery rerolls one Hit Die per Breather.<br>Precision Strike adds FIG to damage when hitting with an attack or Power that deals damage.<br>Exploit the Opening adds an extra Power Die 1x/Turn when target has a Condition, has already been damaged this Turn, or you have Advantage; failed save leaves target Dazed until end of next Turn.</p><p>Gear Dependent: Gadgetry requires gear loadout. Armor Interface powers only function while wearing the suit. Rebuilding or recovering the suit requires Downtime and appropriate resources.</p><p>Doug was on a beer run during the ice-fishing Pulse event and missed the cool stuff.</p>",
    "side": "Heroic",
    "calling": "",
    "triggers": {
      "minor": "Exploit an enemy opening with precision or use armor/gadgets to protect someone in immediate danger.",
      "major": "Take the bold approach against a dangerous threat to keep Detroit civilians, teammates, or Colt safe.",
      "defining": "Lose something significant or suffer defeat because you trusted your suit, gadgets, or own confidence while protecting others."
    },
